<ContentPage
  title="Privacy Policy · Beanie · Tiny Big Labs"
  description="Privacy Policy for Beanie — Tiny Big Labs"
  heading="Privacy Policy for Beanie"
  subheading="Last updated: May 2026"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Beanie is designed with privacy at its core. We do not collect, sell, or share your personal data. There are no accounts, no sign-ins, and no third-party trackers.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data Storage</h2>
    <p>All data you enter into Beanie — including your bean library, coffee spots, flavour notes, and settings — is stored locally on your device using Apple's SwiftData framework. If you have iCloud enabled, this data is synced privately through your personal iCloud account, governed by Apple's Privacy Policy.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>Beanie uses Apple's MetricKit framework to collect anonymous, aggregated performance and crash data. This data is provided to us by Apple and contains no personally identifiable information. It is used solely to improve app stability and performance.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Photos</h2>
    <p>Any photos you add to your bean or coffee spot entries are stored locally on your device and never transmitted to any server.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Third Parties</h2>
    <p>Beanie does not integrate any third-party analytics, advertising, or data collection services.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>If you have any questions about this policy, use the form below to get in touch.</p>
    <form action="https://formspree.io/f/meenvyne" method="POST" class="contact-form">
      <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Your email" required />
      <textarea name="message" placeholder="Your message" rows="4" required></textarea>
      <button type="submit">Send message</button>
    </form>
  </section>
</ContentPage>
